WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.209 --> 00:00:01.161
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:01.161 --> 00:00:04.685
Today, I'm going to share with
you the best way to get a yes

00:00:04.685 --> 00:00:05.852
from an email.

00:00:08.969 --> 00:00:09.802
So as entrepreneurs,

00:00:09.802 --> 00:00:12.110
we do a lot of selling
and marketing via email.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.706
We want our emails to get open,

00:00:13.706 --> 00:00:15.117
we want emails to be responded to,

00:00:15.117 --> 00:00:16.934
we want people to take action,

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.833
every time we send an email out to people.

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:21.294
And when I was doing my
campaign for my book,

00:00:21.294 --> 00:00:22.554
I connected with a lot of people

00:00:22.554 --> 00:00:24.737
who were on the fringe of my network,

00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:25.741
via email.

00:00:25.741 --> 00:00:28.283
I've got a lot of people to
support me and take action,

00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:31.556
and I even got one person
writing back to me saying,

00:00:31.556 --> 00:00:34.656
"This was the single best
written request for support email

00:00:34.656 --> 00:00:36.421
"I've ever seen."

00:00:36.421 --> 00:00:38.244
And this guy has seen a lot.

00:00:38.244 --> 00:00:40.409
It let me get in a
podcast interview with him

00:00:40.409 --> 00:00:43.718
and led to a Forbes article
being written about my book,

00:00:43.718 --> 00:00:45.053
and so it led to a lot of opportunities

00:00:45.053 --> 00:00:49.372
all because I sent one
really well crafted email.

00:00:49.372 --> 00:00:50.580
You guys want to see what I wrote?

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.217
I'm going to share it with you today

00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:53.929
and hopefully you can
learn from it as well

00:00:53.929 --> 00:00:55.729
and apply it to your business.

00:00:55.729 --> 00:00:57.360
So as an extra point of context,

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.193
the guy wrote this too.

00:00:58.193 --> 00:00:59.261
His name is Kevin Kruse.

00:00:59.261 --> 00:01:01.346
I did an interview with him on my channel

00:01:01.346 --> 00:01:02.658
over a year ago.

00:01:02.658 --> 00:01:04.243
I had not been in touch

00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:05.076
since.

00:01:05.076 --> 00:01:06.147
So it's been

00:01:06.147 --> 00:01:07.882
12 months of radio silence,

00:01:07.882 --> 00:01:09.073
and here I was reaching out,

00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:10.408
trying to ask for his support

00:01:10.408 --> 00:01:11.720
in promoting my book.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:12.759
Here's what I wrote.

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:13.592
Hi Kevin.

00:01:13.592 --> 00:01:15.423
Thanks again for the
fun interview last year.

00:01:15.423 --> 00:01:17.374
My fav comment was,

00:01:17.374 --> 00:01:19.533
Incredibly good and informative video.

00:01:19.533 --> 00:01:21.971
Thank you Evan and thank you Mister Kruse.

00:01:21.971 --> 00:01:23.887
You have a new subscription from me.

00:01:23.887 --> 00:01:25.333
This comes at a perfect time.

00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:26.697
I wanted to quickly touch base

00:01:26.697 --> 00:01:28.270
because I just launched my first book

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.861
and I could really use your help.

00:01:29.861 --> 00:01:31.057
It's called Your One Word:

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.537
The powerful secret to creating a business

00:01:32.537 --> 00:01:33.750
and life that matter

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.358
and I've been endorsed by Gary Vaynerchuk,

00:01:35.358 --> 00:01:37.861
Lewis Howes, James Altucher, among others.

00:01:37.861 --> 00:01:39.498
More can be found here.

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:40.508
And I link the website.

00:01:40.508 --> 00:01:43.465
It's about finding your one
word, your one true core value,

00:01:43.465 --> 00:01:45.753
and then building a life
and business around it,

00:01:45.753 --> 00:01:47.587
like I have for around Believe.

00:01:47.587 --> 00:01:48.928
I know it's going to seem greedy of me

00:01:48.928 --> 00:01:50.443
but I was wondering what's the chance

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.929
you could help me reach more people?

00:01:51.929 --> 00:01:52.916
It could be through an article,

00:01:52.916 --> 00:01:54.669
a video, an introduction, or basically

00:01:54.669 --> 00:01:57.223
anything that you think might
help spread the message.

00:01:57.223 --> 00:01:58.715
I'm asking because I respect you

00:01:58.715 --> 00:02:00.892
and also believe in the
message of the book so much

00:02:00.892 --> 00:02:02.430
that anyone you connect it to

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.067
will be immediately thankful.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.176
If not, I totally get it.

00:02:05.176 --> 00:02:07.521
And I'm happy to support
your work in the future.

00:02:07.521 --> 00:02:08.354
So that was the email.

00:02:08.354 --> 00:02:09.774
I'm reading it on my phone here.

00:02:09.774 --> 00:02:11.022
Let me break down

00:02:11.022 --> 00:02:12.200
the different elements of it

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.984
to explain why it works so well.

00:02:13.984 --> 00:02:15.435
So at the start, I'm just thanking him.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.183
Thanks again for the
fun interview last year.

00:02:17.183 --> 00:02:19.046
Kind of reminding the point of context.

00:02:19.046 --> 00:02:20.323
He may have forgotten about me.

00:02:20.323 --> 00:02:21.751
He may not remember who I am.

00:02:21.751 --> 00:02:23.377
Quite often we meet so many people

00:02:23.377 --> 00:02:24.584
in the course of a year

00:02:24.584 --> 00:02:26.482
that it's easy to forget some people.

00:02:26.482 --> 00:02:27.315
And so,

00:02:27.315 --> 00:02:28.595
if you've met them at an event

00:02:28.595 --> 00:02:30.551
or you had coffee, you
had a quick phone call,

00:02:30.551 --> 00:02:31.678
or you've have been exchanging emails,

00:02:31.678 --> 00:02:32.921
and it's been a long time,

00:02:32.921 --> 00:02:33.885
just reminding them

00:02:33.885 --> 00:02:36.195
the context of which you're reaching out,

00:02:36.195 --> 00:02:37.902
how you guys have already met before,

00:02:37.902 --> 00:02:39.858
or if you're being
introduced by somebody else,

00:02:39.858 --> 00:02:41.861
putting that on their radar immediately,

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.109
so they know where you're coming from.

00:02:43.109 --> 00:02:44.798
Next up, I share a comment.

00:02:44.798 --> 00:02:46.331
And I did this for
everybody that I interviewed

00:02:46.331 --> 00:02:48.438
over the past couple years on my channel.

00:02:48.438 --> 00:02:50.081
I tried to share one good thing

00:02:50.081 --> 00:02:51.410
to make him feel

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:52.243
really good.

00:02:52.243 --> 00:02:53.430
So this person left a comment.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.292
It was a good and informative video

00:02:55.292 --> 00:02:57.365
thanking us, we got a new subscription.

00:02:57.365 --> 00:02:59.489
And so, I wanted to make him feel good

00:02:59.489 --> 00:03:01.585
about that thing that we did a year ago

00:03:01.585 --> 00:03:03.239
reminding him about how good it was,

00:03:03.239 --> 00:03:04.322
again, in case he forgot.

00:03:04.322 --> 00:03:05.486
Then I wanted to get into the book

00:03:05.486 --> 00:03:07.675
and I explained quickly what it was about.

00:03:07.675 --> 00:03:09.091
I explained who had endorsed it,

00:03:09.091 --> 00:03:10.572
I explained a little bit of the content

00:03:10.572 --> 00:03:12.401
and it provided a length
more of information,

00:03:12.401 --> 00:03:13.452
in case he cared.

00:03:13.452 --> 00:03:14.827
I didn't want to get into

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.347
three pages long about
why the book is so great,

00:03:17.347 --> 00:03:19.204
just a quick statement about what it is,

00:03:19.204 --> 00:03:21.103
what it's called, who's endorsed it,

00:03:21.103 --> 00:03:23.518
and then a link to find
out more information.

00:03:23.518 --> 00:03:24.644
So after I introduced the book,

00:03:24.644 --> 00:03:26.025
I wanted to ask for help.

00:03:26.025 --> 00:03:28.179
The next line I pulled from Lewis Howes'

00:03:28.179 --> 00:03:29.255
YouTube channel,

00:03:29.255 --> 00:03:32.472
you have this great guy on
who's an FBI negotiator,

00:03:32.472 --> 00:03:34.651
and this was the line
that he recommends using

00:03:34.651 --> 00:03:37.089
in business negotiations, saying,

00:03:37.089 --> 00:03:38.450
"I know it's going to seem greedy of me,

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.283
"but I was wondering

00:03:39.283 --> 00:03:41.517
"what's the chance you could
help me reach more people?"

00:03:41.517 --> 00:03:43.258
And that disarms them

00:03:43.258 --> 00:03:45.371
and opens them up to be willing to help.

00:03:45.371 --> 00:03:46.204
Then I was just trying to give some

00:03:46.204 --> 00:03:47.073
examples.

00:03:47.073 --> 00:03:48.141
So it could be through an article,

00:03:48.141 --> 00:03:49.244
a video, an introduction,

00:03:49.244 --> 00:03:51.877
anything that you think might
help spread the message.

00:03:51.877 --> 00:03:53.900
I don't want to be so specific and say,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.750
"To your newsletter list."

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.675
Because one, maybe he doesn't
have a newsletter list

00:03:56.675 --> 00:03:59.114
or two, maybe he doesn't
want to send it out

00:03:59.114 --> 00:04:00.165
to his newsletter list.

00:04:00.165 --> 00:04:01.656
Basically, anything that he could think of

00:04:01.656 --> 00:04:02.719
to help me with the book,

00:04:02.719 --> 00:04:03.839
I would really appreciate it.

00:04:03.839 --> 00:04:05.279
Then I flatter him a little bit, right?

00:04:05.279 --> 00:04:06.939
I'm asking because I respect you

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:08.588
and also believe in the
message of the book so much

00:04:08.588 --> 00:04:10.927
that anyone you connect it to will be

00:04:10.927 --> 00:04:11.966
immediately thankful.

00:04:11.966 --> 00:04:13.156
There's a lot of value in the book,

00:04:13.156 --> 00:04:14.306
and really respect him.

00:04:14.306 --> 00:04:16.732
And then I end on it
not being a hard sell.

00:04:16.732 --> 00:04:18.305
So, if not, I totally get it

00:04:18.305 --> 00:04:21.306
and I'm happy to support
your work in the future.

00:04:21.306 --> 00:04:22.139
And so,

00:04:22.139 --> 00:04:23.129
not forcing him to do it,

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.393
showing that I really respect
his time and his opinion,

00:04:25.393 --> 00:04:27.947
and I'll be really
grateful for his support.

00:04:27.947 --> 00:04:29.578
And so this really helped me

00:04:29.578 --> 00:04:30.577
get a lot of endorsements

00:04:30.577 --> 00:04:31.569
get a lot of support

00:04:31.569 --> 00:04:32.562
get a lot of introductions,

00:04:32.562 --> 00:04:33.395
get a lot of connections

00:04:33.395 --> 00:04:34.803
and also Kevin

00:04:34.803 --> 00:04:35.926
himself

00:04:35.926 --> 00:04:38.134
saying that it was the single best request

00:04:38.134 --> 00:04:39.879
for a support email he's ever seen

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.645
and that leading to his podcast interview

00:04:41.645 --> 00:04:43.526
and the Forbes interview as well.

00:04:43.526 --> 00:04:45.945
And so, hopefully you can
learn from that structure.

00:04:45.945 --> 00:04:47.418
Apply it to your emails

00:04:47.418 --> 00:04:49.075
and get a much better result

00:04:49.075 --> 00:04:50.511
when you're sending it off to

00:04:50.511 --> 00:04:53.155
customers, partners, investors, suppliers,

00:04:53.155 --> 00:04:56.226
potential influences to
help get your message out.

00:04:56.226 --> 00:04:58.352
So that's how I sell via email

00:04:58.352 --> 00:04:59.831
with a quick template and an example.

00:04:59.831 --> 00:05:00.664
We'll link up the text

00:05:00.664 --> 00:05:01.797
in the description below

00:05:01.797 --> 00:05:04.017
so you guys can copy and
paste and tweak around

00:05:04.017 --> 00:05:05.104
like you want to.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.828
I love to know what
did you take from this?

00:05:06.828 --> 00:05:08.473
What did you enjoy most about this email?

00:05:08.473 --> 00:05:10.871
Do you have any other email
secrets, tips, strategies

00:05:10.871 --> 00:05:11.916
that you want to share?

00:05:11.916 --> 00:05:13.535
Please leave that in the comments below.

00:05:13.535 --> 00:05:14.794
I'm curious to find out.

00:05:14.794 --> 00:05:15.925
Finally I want to take
up a quick shout out

00:05:15.925 --> 00:05:17.669
to David VandenBloomen Junior.

00:05:17.669 --> 00:05:20.182
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:05:20.182 --> 00:05:21.070
Your One Word.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.867
It really, really,
really, means a lot to me.

00:05:22.867 --> 00:05:24.204
And I hope you're enjoying it.

00:05:24.204 --> 00:05:25.929
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:25.929 --> 00:05:27.010
I Believe in you.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.906
I hope you continue to Believe in yourself

00:05:28.906 --> 00:05:31.012
and whatever your one word is,

00:05:31.012 --> 00:05:32.266
much love,

00:05:32.266 --> 00:05:33.766
I'll see you soon.

